WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.600
Ancient India.

2
00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:05.260
A group of women shave their
heads and walk to Vesali.

3
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.590
Their leader, Mahapajapati, the
Buddha's aunt and foster mother,

4
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.770
asks to go forth as a nun.

5
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.490
Three times, the Buddha refuses.

6
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.740
Today, fully ordained nuns are
a familiar sight in Taiwan.

7
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:22.710
In Thailand, a woman seeking
the same faces a struggle.

8
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.040
So why can a woman become a
fully ordained nun in Taiwan,

9
00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:28.430
but not easily in Thailand?

10
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.820
In this mission, you'll see how
the first nuns' order began,

11
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.990
with eight weighty rules.

12
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.640
Then you'll meet the women
campaigning for change,

13
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:39.120
and weigh the arguments on both sides.

14
00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:43.040
Your mission: explain why Taiwan's
nuns can be fully ordained,

15
00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.320
while Thai women struggle to be.
